## Commands
- Test: `{{TEST_CMD}}`
- Lint: `{{LINT_CMD}}`
- Build: `{{BUILD_CMD}}`
- Start the app (dev): `{{START_CMD}}`
- E2E (real app): `{{E2E_CMD}}`
- Screenshot: `{{SCREENSHOT_CMD}}` <!-- <screen-id> [--theme light|dark] [--size WxH] --out <path> -->
- Package (unsigned, local OS): `{{PACKAGE_CMD}}`
<!-- TBD means not set yet: /scaffold fills these in. From WSL, Windows-side commands run through scripts/win-run.sh. -->

## Verifying your work
Run test, lint and build before reporting any task complete, and paste the output. For UI, also run e2e and the screenshots on each local OS.
If a test fails, fix the code, not the test. Never skip or delete a failing test, and never skip it on one OS.
Never claim an OS was verified unless the check actually ran on that OS (locally or in CI).

## How work flows here
- App level: /define or /clone → product/definition.md → /prototype app → /roadmap → /scaffold (R-1).
- Per feature: work items live in `work/<date>-<slug>/`: intent.md → prototype/ → spec.md → plan.md → verify.md.
- Prototype: {{PROTOTYPE}}
- Skills: /define, /clone, /roadmap, /scaffold, /intent, /prototype, /spec, /build, /fix, /ship, /release, /triage.
- Files listed in `work/*/locks.txt` or `product/locks.txt` were approved by a person; never edit them.
- Signing certificates, passwords and updater keys live only in CI secrets; never in the repo.

## Issues
- Tracker: {{TRACKER}}
- Status updates: {{STATUS_UPDATES}}
- Triage: {{TRIAGE}}
